{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:51fafbe3529f350f","name":"CF9 Crossfire Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-51fafbe3529f350f","title":"CF9 Crossfire Starfighter","revision":20111,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:14:15Z","sha256":"00c1a6c87daacdba34383f62b22559b9a3a14f9545f42af4f78a403082d74b44","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20111","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=CF9%20Crossfire%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-51fafbe3529f350f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:bd53073ee6d4d9a0"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["After more than a hundred years of success with the crossed-wing design featured in a multitude of ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-Wing"}," variants, a new design team at Incom incorporated the concept into a mainline Starfighter designed specifically for ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:bd53073ee6d4d9a0"},". Due to strict government requirements, as well as advancements in engine technology and armor composition, the ship would not be a direct descendant in terms of technology or styling. In keeping with The Galactic Alliance's design philosophy of packing more power into smaller ships, the Crossfire is a much smaller fighter, aside from its signature wings. However, Incom also took the trademark crossed-wing design in a new direction.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The deployment system for the Crossfire's S-foils is mounted at the ship's bow, in front of the cockpit. Both wing sections remain horizontal in flight and landing mode, but the trailing wing section rotates to a vertical position when entering combat, while the forward section remain horizontal. The vertical wing is therefore directly in the middle of the pilot's forward view, but the wings amazingly thin profile minimizes the obstruction. The resulting gun orientation creates a laser intersection point far ahead of the fighter, making it devastating at longer ranges than fighters with twin guns mounted side-by-side.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ship features a compact yet powerful Coldstar ion tri-engine core mounted in a heavily armored pod. Combined with the fighter's relatively small size, it provides the ship with excellent acceleration and maneuverability. Pilots love the Crossfire's ability to take punishment. Much of the fighter's durability is due to its heavily armored cockpit and fuselage shroud. While the armored canopy limits the pilot's view, the heads-up displays and combat sensor packs more than compensate.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Crossfire is capable of operating independently of a carrier thanks to its built-in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"},". It is one of the smallest ships with a fully capable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputer","referenceId":"reference:4ae152610571a224"},", thereby eliminating the need for an Astromech Droid for hyperspace navigation. While some pilots miss the companionship of the Droid, most find that the new systems provide just as much information as a Droid, without the personality quirks.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Finally, the Crossfire is actually a two-seater, allowing a Gunner or passenger to ride along in the aft facing seat, like the Rebel ",{"tag":"a","children":["T-47 Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T-47_Airspeeders"}," of old. However, most ships are flown solo, as the limited firing arc of the aft-mounted ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannon","referenceId":"reference:0911ab4bc0e93386"}," reduces their effectiveness. Combined with the typical radical maneuvers performed in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dogfighting"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dogfighting"},", this leaves the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," with few opportunities to effectively contribute to a battle. Enemy pilots soon learn to ignore the aft cannon, but this can occasionally get them into trouble, should a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," actually be on board. Additionally, the fighter is designed to be adapted quickly to pilots of many ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", though some of the larger ones may find the small cockpit a bit cramped.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["CF9 Crossfire Starfighter Statistics (CL 12)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +9; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 21 (",{"tag":"a","childre